From 8b4d76deda406e5132257d44f3dfb6dd45f5f50c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anisetti Avinash Krishna <anisetti.avinash.krishna@intel.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:29:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Switch WCL SOF topology to modular function-topology files

Upstream kernel 6.18.38 removed the single-device rt722 match-table
entries (ptl_rt722_only/l1/l3) in
sound/soc/intel/common/soc-acpi-intel-ptl-match.c that previously
selected the legacy monolithic sof-ptl-rt722.tplg for WCL's standalone
rt722 SoundWire codec. Only an aggregated-device variant remains, so
WCL now always falls through to the generic default machine driver,
which unconditionally requires the modular "function topology"
scheme (one file per DAI-link function) instead of a single topology
file.

Replace sof-ptl-rt722.tplg with the four modular topology files SOF
actually requests for this board's DAI links (jack, amp, mic, HDMI),
taken from the matching sof-bin v2.14.x release (same ADSPFW version,
2.14.1.1, as the already-shipped sof-wcl.ri):
- sof-sdca-jack-id0.tplg
- sof-sdca-1amp-id2.tplg
- sof-sdca-mic-id4.tplg
- sof-hdmi-pcm5-id5.tplg

Verified on WCL SODIMM RVP: sofsoundwire card now registers
successfully (previously fell back to the Dummy ALSA card with
'error: failed to load DSP topology -22').

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1695
Signed-off-by: Anisetti Avinash Krishna <anisetti.avinash.krishna@intel.com>
---
 intel/sof-ipc4-tplg/sof-hdmi-pcm5-id5.tplg | Bin 0 -> 15394 bytes
 intel/sof-ipc4-tplg/sof-ptl-rt722.tplg     | Bin 59994 -> 0 bytes
 intel/sof-ipc4-tplg/sof-sdca-1amp-id2.tplg | Bin 0 -> 12102 bytes
 intel/sof-ipc4-tplg/sof-sdca-jack-id0.tplg | Bin 0 -> 20862 bytes
 intel/sof-ipc4-tplg/sof-sdca-mic-id4.tplg  | Bin 0 -> 12422 bytes
 5 files changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 intel/sof-ipc4-tplg/sof-hdmi-pcm5-id5.tplg
 delete mode 100644 intel/sof-ipc4-tplg/sof-ptl-rt722.tplg
